    <id>http://arxiv.org/abs/1301.3303v1</id>
    <title>Modular forms, hypergeometric functions and congruences</title>
    <updated>2013-01-15T10:58:29Z</updated>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1301.3303v1" rel="alternate" type="text/html"/>
    <link href="https://arxiv.org/pdf/1301.3303v1" rel="related" type="application/pdf" title="pdf"/>
    <summary>Using the theory of Stienstra and Beukers, we prove various elementary congruences for the numbers \sum \binom{2i_1}{i_1}^2\binom{2i_2}{i_2}^2...\binom{2i_k}{i_k}^2, where k,n \in N, and the summation is over the integers i_1, i_2, ...i_k &gt;= 0 such that i_1+i_2+...+i_k=n. To obtain that, we study the arithmetic properties of Fourier coefficients of certain (weakly holomorphic) modular forms.</summary>
